      "date": "2026-11-04 06:03:46.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(1 comment)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nLooks good, the fix is correct and fine to land as is. One optional suggestion: a dryrun regression test would help. Running a variant of sanity-lfsck test_2a (OBD_FAIL_LFSCK_LINKEA_CRASH, so lfsck_links_read() returns -EINVAL and lfsck_namespace_links_remove() is called) with `lfsck_start -n on`, then checking that the linkEA is left unchanged and the inconsistency is still counted, would have caught this. The bug went unnoticed after 441902fa3d44 because nothing exercises that path in dryrun mode.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    }
